<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marriage of the Sea ceremony</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Sposalizio del Mare</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Marriage of the Sea was a maritime ceremony of the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>, held on Ascension Day, in which the doge threw a golden ring into the Adriatic Sea as a sign of Venice's dominion over it. According to most authors it first appeared around the year 1000, at the time of the Venetian conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalmatia">Dalmatia</a> under Doge <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pietro-ii-orseolo">Pietro II Orseolo</a>; it was fixed on Ascension Day in 1173 under Doge Sebastiano Ziani. The doge sailed out on the state galley, the bucentaur, with the Senate, and the Patriarch of Venice pronounced a nuptial blessing. It lasted until the fall of the Republic in 1797, and the mayor of Venice has re-enacted it since 1965.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marriage-of-the-sea-ceremony.jpg" alt="Marriage of the Sea ceremony" width="330" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Francesco Guardi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Francesco_Guardi_021.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
